--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/knowledge-boundary-rollback.md
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+# Knowledge boundary rollback plan
+
+The Catalog boundary is an API-only extraction; it does not convert or alter the
+`documents`, `embeddings`, or `deliveries` tables. If rollout reveals a problem,
+rollback is safe and reversible:
+
+1. Revert the delivery caller to the previous response implementation (or deploy
+a version before this change).
+2. Keep the existing tables and records in place; no migration or data rollback is
+needed.
+3. The Catalog implementation can continue to read the same published rows, or
+be removed with the pack if the prior release is restored.
+4. Re-run the endpoint characterization and job tests before retrying.
+
+No persistence conversion is part of this change. Any future persistence change
+must first add characterization coverage and an independently tested rollback.
